## What shipped

#811, all three defects in `generate_commit_message`:

1. **`.contains("test") → path_is_test** — matches by path *shape*, language-agnostic (Kind: product, so not "Rust files under src/`"): components tests/test/spec/__tests__, stems ending _test/_tests, filenames containing .test./.spec.. src/commands_latest.rs no longer matches; `src/main_tests.rs` does.
2. First-match ladder → dominant match — commit_file_category + dominant_commit_category, weighted by per-file changed lines parsed out of the diff already being walked (no new git invocation; a rename still weighs 1). Ties go to production code. Prefix vocabulary unchanged (test/docs/chore/refactor/feat).
3. Summary no longer empties out when the commit is biggest — past 3 files it names the file carrying the most changed lines instead of update code. Under 4 files the strings are byte-identical to before.

Verbatim result for the #811 file list: `feat(6 files): update prompt (+5 more)`

Tests (at the emission point, on the string the caller receives): the mixed fixture+production case that produced #811, the substring near-miss, the real-test-path near-miss guard, a cross-language table for path_is_test, and a tie table for dominant_commit_category. All four pre-existing tests kept — test_generate_commit_message_multiple_files was pinning the degradation, so its "4 files" assertion stands and two were added beside a comment explaining what changed.

## One thing I had to decide mid-task

The module-size gate fired: git.rs was already at 1997/2000 and this landed 259 lines past the cap — far outside the 50-line grace band, which is precisely the design event that gate exists for. Registering 259 lines of debt when a clean seam was sitting right there would have been the ceiling-as-furniture move my own notes warn about. So I split: src/git_commit_msg.rs is a pure move (no body rewritten), re-exported from git.rs so every call site still says git::generate_commit_message. git.rs 1997 → 1848.

